+## Notification API
+
+`services/notification/app.py`, port 8003 (Order calls it via `toxiproxy:18003`). Does not send real email yet; it only stores each notification in its own `notifications` database.
+
+Order sends the confirmation from a background task after an order becomes `CONFIRMED` and the checkout had a `customer_email`. It is best-effort: up to 5 attempts with backoff, and a Notification outage never slows or fails a checkout (if all attempts fail, the notification is lost). Failed orders and checkouts without an email send nothing.
+
+| Method | Path | What it does |
+|---|---|---|
+| POST | `/notifications` | `{"order_id", "recipient", "message"}`. 201 when stored; one notification per `order_id`, so a repeat returns the stored one (200, `"replayed": true`). Invalid recipient → 422 |
+| GET | `/notifications?order_id=` | Stored notifications (`id`, `order_id`, `recipient`, `message`, `created_at`), optionally for one order |
+| POST | `/admin/reset` | Delete all notifications |
+| GET | `/health` | `{"status": "ok"}` if the DB is reachable |
